--- The ceilings of [`build.tree_checks`]'s `checked`: how many errors of each code of [`lang.check`] each file of the
--- tree has in its bodies, which the new checker's expressions report and no rewrite or later piece has removed yet.
--- A key is `<file> <code>`. A file with more errors of a code than pinned is refused, and one with fewer is told to
--- lower its pin. A rewrite or a later piece only lowers pins. A change that adds or sharpens a rule of the checker may
--- raise some, or add some for a new code, and says why in its message: the places the rule newly refuses, and the lines
--- it adds to the files it edits. The pins below are grouped by code, with the rule or the later piece that brings each
--- to zero.
local record CheckPins
  pins: {string: integer}
end

